2026-10-02T13:36:41.506Z [DEBUG] Tool invocation result: [{"author_association":"NONE","body":"##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n * Feature Idea\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n* DNS\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n/\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n* for customer isolated network\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n/\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\nFor adaptive computing it's important to get use of additional application local IP addresses which you can move between machines in case of a failure of one of the virtual machines or for upgrades.\r\n\r\nI can attach an additional IP to a VM using ACS. But I cannot give that a separate name which does not belong to the actual hostname of the VM.\r\n\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n* possibility to add a DNS name for the additional local IP address\r\n* possibility to move an IP from one system to another (no delete and recreate - IP could be taken in the steps between)\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n* currently the additional IP resolves into the same name as the original IP which is the hostname","comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/2865/comments","created_at":"2018-09-27T15:48:32Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/2865/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/2865","id":364540980,"labels":[{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"l